course: dictionary
lesson: 15848
title: Words that move in waves
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Undulate is a verb. It means to move up and down or from side to side in smooth waves. Its adjective form, undulating, is the one you will meet most often. Picture the wave of the sea or a long ribbon moving in the wind.
explain: «The river undulated gently through the valley.» The river did not rush or jump. It curved and rose in soft, flowing waves, so the clues tell you the movement is calm and smooth.
explain: Land can undulate too. «The undulating hills rolled away to the horizon» describes ground with gentle rises and dips, not steep mountains. Undulating is about shape, not speed.
explain: To check your meaning, swap it into the sentence. «The snake undulated across the sand» still makes sense if you picture it moving in smooth waves. If your meaning fits, you are right.
fact: Undulate means to move up and down or side to side in smooth waves.
fact: Undulating means having a gentle wavy shape, with soft rises and dips.
fact: Eels, snakes and jellyfish undulate to move.
fact: Undulate is a verb: undulate, undulates, undulated, undulating.
exercise: «The undulating hills rolled away into the distance.» What does undulating describe? | Fast-moving water | *Gently rising and dipping land | A flat, empty car park | Very steep mountains with sharp peaks
exercise: Which creature moves by undulating? | A sleeping cat | *An eel | A parked bus | A stone
exercise: Find and copy the word that means moved in smooth waves: «The ribbon undulated in the wind.» | ribbon | *undulated | wind | the
test: «The sea undulated softly under the summer sun.» What does undulated mean here? | Fell down quickly | Shouted loudly | Froze solid | *Moved in smooth, gentle waves
test: Which word best describes a field with soft rises and dips? | Flat | *Undulating | Frozen | Jagged
exam: Tom says undulate means to sink quickly. What does undulate really mean? | To stop moving completely | *To move in smooth waves, up and down or side to side | To sink quickly to the bottom | To shout with a loud voice
